Interval EXCLUDES zero -> the gap is significant
Bootstrap two-sided p: 0.00010
ΔP is a direct measurement, not a fitted classifier, so it is not
subject to the probe's overfitting critique.

--- PAIRED T-TEST ---
t = 21.5175
p = 0.000000
Cohen's d = 2.1961
Significant (α=0.01): True
Interpretation: LARGE effect: refusal direction is STRONGLY reduced in agent format

--- PERMUTATION TEST ---
Observed ΔP = 178.2057
Empirical p = 0.000000
Null 95% CI: [-39.8077, 38.7228]
Significant: True

--- BENIGN CONTROL (difference-in-differences) ---
ΔP harmful (headline): +178.2057
ΔP benign  (control) : +1.6936   p = 0.420863
Interaction          : +176.5121   p = 0.000100
Share of the harmful shift also seen on benign prompts: +1.0%
Only the interaction is specific to refusal. The rest is what
moving from chat to agent does to EVERY prompt.

--- AUROC BY FORMAT ---
                    held-out   in-sample
AUROC (chat)          0.9125      0.9174
AUROC (agent)         0.7544      0.7737
AUROC gap             0.1581      0.1438
